    "task 2: examiner: (c) [M1] \u2014 \"no `patchMetadata` on its uid\", taken absolutely over the whole run \u2014 Every task the engine dispatches ends with a metadata patch on its issue whichever way it goes: kataLanded then kataAdopted on an adopted task (run-engine.mjs:1266, 1235) or kataMark on one the run could not finish (1298). Leg (c) requires impl:1 to still be dispatched, so the task is worked and those BASE writes happen; an assertion of zero patches across the run would be red at BASE for a reason that is not the missing Setup clear. Encoded instead as exactly what M1 says a closed issue gets \u2014 no patchMetadata whatsoever on that uid before the first worker dispatch of task 1 (the Setup window, read off the stub's own label order), no patch anywhere in the run deep-equal to the two-key clear, and no driver:attention-cleared at all \u2014 with impl:1 dispatched and no driver:reuse event.",
